From: r36max2 <build@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] onscripter: link the Lua that FindLua actually located

CMakeLists.txt:57 names the library `lua`, which is the Arch-style soname. On
Ubuntu the lua5.4-dev package installs liblua5.4.so and no liblua.so, so cmake
reports "Found Lua: .../liblua5.4.so (5.4.8)", the compile succeeds, and the link
dies on ld.bfd: cannot find -llua. The variable two lines above already holds the
absolute path FindLua resolved, so link that instead of a name the distro does not
ship.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
             SDL2::SDL2
             jpeg
             bz2
-            lua
+            ${LUA_LIBRARIES}
             dl
             SDL2_ttf
             SDL2_image
